The fleet has a growth member, with send limits it cannot talk its way past

The fleet can now run go-to-market: the growth member sends outreach/marketing
email with hard policy limits enforced in code, never in prompts.

New behavior:
1. Growth member (members/growth/): owns awareness and sign-ups via email, content,
   and search. Disabled by default. Reports what moved via access logs.
2. Send tool (scripts/outreach_send.py): the ONLY path for marketing/outreach mail.
   Enforces before any send: policy enabled, daily/per-recipient caps, GDPR consent,
   list source allowed, email type allowed, recipient not unsubscribed.
3. Configuration (fleet.env): outreach policy as environment variables
   (enabled flag, sending domain, caps in units and USD, GDPR region rules,
   allowed sources and email types). All OFF by default.
4. Database schema (fleet_db.py): outreach_campaigns, recipients, results, ledger
   for measuring compliance post-hoc.
5. Ledger: every send decision (sent/refused + reason) logged to fleet.db for
   audit and measuring what stopped what.
6. Ask.py configurable: FLEET_ASK_MAIL_FROM env var makes the "from" address
   configurable, preserving hello@philanthropy.org as the live default.

Tests prove:
- Every cap actually refuses (daily, spend, daily per-recipient)
- Every refusal reason works (GDPR consent, list source, email type, suppression)
- Member spec validates and is disabled by default
- Dry-run walkthrough shows footer + ledger + compliance

No real email sent. Dry-run is default; real send requires --send flag AND
policy enabled in fleet.env. Unsubscribe handling: link in every mail, immediate
addition to suppression list.

